Help For The Receive Audio Setup

Receive audio setup: full stop next input; comma previous; c cycles physical input channels. v checks the selected channel level for one second without playing it. e saves the choice; q Back. h help. No input opens until you request v; e validates supported format without capture. Device names and host audio system are announced. Several entries may refer to the same physical input through different host systems. Choose the radio, not your microphone. The level check only detects audio; it cannot prove which device is the radio. Receive a steady signal and compare levels/channels. Channel numbers do not guarantee Main/Sub. Saved name and host must uniquely match on later use; missing or duplicate devices fail without fallback. Setup never changes Windows defaults, screen-reader output or playback devices. Existing audio decoding stops when setup opens; restart it explicitly afterwards. Optional sounddevice/PortAudio is required. Changes are saved only with e; q does not save your current browsing choice.

